<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n32407" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">offulgĕo</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">obf-</span></b> ), si, 2, v. n.
		ob-fulgeo, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>to shine against</i> or <i>upon; to
				appear</i> (not ante-Aug.). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">continuo nova lux oculis offulsit,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Verg.
					A. 9, 110</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">dextrum offulsit conatibus omen,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Sil.
					13, 114</span></i>
			: species mei amici, Ps. -<i><span class="en">Quint.
				Decl. 9, 7</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Trop.</b>: lucrum, Ps. -<i><span class="en">Quint.
				Decl. 12, 4</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ortus imperii nostri,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cod. Theod. 2, 8, 25</span></i>
			.</div>
